  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening Peaceful Coexistence, Community Integration and Institutional Response to Cross-Border Communities in the Northern Zone of Costa Rica Affected by Human Mobility</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project focuses on addressing the tensions created by xenophobia and hate speech to prevent the escalation of conflicts which could result in incitement to discrimination, hostility, and direct, cultural, and systematic violence. The project will counter the root causes of these conflicts by creating safe spaces for intercultural dialogue at the municipal and national level, and by strengthening local actors&#x2019; capabilities to promote the integration and protection of migrants and asylum seekers.  Project activities will be implemented in the Northern Region of Costa Rica, specifically in the cantons Guatuso, Upala and Los Chiles at the border with Nicaragua.</narrative>
  </description>
